---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";

const props = {
	title: "Readmissions ML Pipeline",
	tagline:
		"Scores healthcare providers on hospital readmissions and forecasts where the trend is heading.",
	description:
		"LightGBM scoring on about 650K insurance claims with forecasts, an Airflow and Spark pipeline and Power BI dashboards.",
	status: "shipped" as const,
	startDate: "2025",
	type: "product" as const,
	role: "AI engineering co-op",
	stack: ["LightGBM", "Spark", "Hive", "Impala", "Apache Airflow", "Power BI"],
	relatedProjects: [{ slug: "policy-rag-agent", title: "Policy RAG Agent" }],
};
---

<ProjectLayout {...props}>
	<h2>The question</h2>
	<p>
		Built during my co-op at a Saudi health-insurance regulator: which
		providers send patients back into hospital more than they should, and
		where is that trend heading next quarter?
	</p>

	<h2>What I built</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Scoring model:</strong> LightGBM on about 650K claim records with heavy class imbalance (about 10% readmissions). Validation F1 0.79 and ROC-AUC 0.73, turned into provider-level observed/expected ratios.</li>
		<li><strong>Forecasting:</strong> exponential smoothing on readmission and length-of-stay time series.</li>
		<li><strong>Pipeline:</strong> Spark, Hive and Impala for ingestion and features, orchestrated with Apache Airflow.</li>
		<li><strong>Dashboard:</strong> a bilingual Power BI dashboard for non-technical stakeholders, with top and bottom providers, common readmission diagnoses and actuals vs forecast.</li>
	</ul>
</ProjectLayout>
